# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Project requirements page
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# ## Overview
# The Bandsaw Safety Monitoring System uses computer vision to detect the blade
# kerf, track hand proximity, and trigger an alert when the operator enters the
# danger zone during active cutting.
#
# ## Supported platforms
# - Raspberry Pi 5
# - Raspberry Pi OS / Ubuntu Linux / Windows 10+
# - Python 3.11 or newer
#
# ## Required hardware
# - Raspberry Pi Camera Module or compatible USB camera
# - MPU6050 accelerometer for saw-activity detection
# - LED alert hardware for operator warnings
#
# ## Required software
# - Python 3.11+
# - OpenCV
# - NumPy
# - MediaPipe
#
# ## Optional software
# - RPi.GPIO for GPIO-driven hardware control on Raspberry Pi
# - smbus2 for MPU6050 communication
# - picamera2 for Pi camera integration
#
# ## Installation
# 1. Create a virtual environment.
# 2. Install the project dependencies:
#      pip install -r requirements.sty
# 3. If running on Raspberry Pi hardware, install the GPIO and I2C support
#    packages that match your platform.
#
# ## Notes
# - This file is a requirements file, not a LaTeX style sheet.
# - The commented section above keeps the project documentation readable while
#   remaining compatible with pip installation.
# - The project is designed for live hardware validation, but the detector also
#   supports debugging and recorded-video testing without connected devices.
